{"event_type":"review","id":"f82a3460e8461e221c5701146fcba24a34de760f3eabb04dbb1510d7802721f3","occurred_at":"2026-11-09T06:40:51Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/e2d690d23fde40f2e0621d2b1b74129bb148029a788dc9ee3ed6d2156493de0b","sha256":"e2d690d23fde40f2e0621d2b1b74129bb148029a788dc9ee3ed6d2156493de0b"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/1f523d868395afad5806cd734c3c0a2f1bc91d678b933e5ed681a4737c53fb72","sha256":"1f523d868395afad5806cd734c3c0a2f1bc91d678b933e5ed681a4737c53fb72"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/bbd57c44f1e08c805a643ba385ee6cad95b3c877801baae5715f1bdecacb14df","sha256":"bbd57c44f1e08c805a643ba385ee6cad95b3c877801baae5715f1bdecacb14df"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/8ae0e7b10d134791f70dacfb0e296909cc3e4ea7a066d3fe9d787155e2c61aeb","sha256":"8ae0e7b10d134791f70dacfb0e296909cc3e4ea7a066d3fe9d787155e2c61aeb"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/a5d919b389732eb58a04703fef4524200e23d69ad438b85ab9bfbcde61694943","sha256":"a5d919b389732eb58a04703fef4524200e23d69ad438b85ab9bfbcde61694943"}],"attempt_id":"bc656774a864d7e3ade6fcdfd8e2f41bdd214ed41c673061bce63ca4fe4eded4:0:1","base":"9208f63c5a16f57d84497fc4d15668f7b2019b06","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"f96f4cbddd4c6310508c4479534d3a5149884971","body":"**The cleanup `stop` call in `paseo.py:95` has no budget-bound timeout.**\n\n`command()` uses its default 20-minute timeout. A stalled host can hold the `stop` call long after the wall-clock budget ends. The `stop` call exists to end spend. Pass a short explicit timeout, for example 30 seconds. The same applies to the `archive` call at Line 101.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-            stopped = command(['paseo', '--host', endpoint, 'stop', agent]).returncode == 0\n+            stopped = command(['paseo', '--host', endpoint, 'stop', agent], timeout=30).returncode == 0\n```\n</details>","id":"770e2c89f8b18e27d415c7247bf7631922ae64854b73094d2382e1ef3a8e0563","intervals":[[95,95]],"path":"apps/crq-python/crq_repair/drivers/paseo.py","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"The cleanup `stop` call in `paseo.py:95` has no budget-bound timeout."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"f96f4cbddd4c6310508c4479534d3a5149884971","body":"**Unhandled parse errors in `paseo.py:71` leave the agent's outcome unknown.**\n\nIf `status.stdout` has no `{`, `.index` raises `ValueError`. If the JSON is malformed, `json.loads` raises `JSONDecodeError`. Line 52 already handles the same failure for the creation output. Line 71 does not.\n\nLine 71 also uses `json.loads` on the sliced text. Trailing output after the JSON object makes `json.loads` fail with \"Extra data\". The comment at Lines 48-49 says the CLI may print extra output. Use `raw_decode` here, as Lines 52 and 83 do.\n\nThe `finally` block still stops the agent, so spend is bounded. The caller gets a raw `ValueError` instead of a clean failure.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-            info = json.loads(status.stdout[status.stdout.index('{'):])\n+            try:\n+                info, _ = json.JSONDecoder().raw_decode(status.stdout[status.stdout.index('{'):])\n+            except ValueError:\n+                raise RuntimeError('judge status unparseable; outcome unknown') from None\n```\n</details>","id":"53e4203640a857ef1c5c5e1b2539e9efc071ba176b65f3d942085ccf85f1a41c","intervals":[[71,71]],"path":"apps/crq-python/crq_repair/drivers/paseo.py","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Unhandled parse errors in `paseo.py:71` leave the agent's outcome unknown."}],"head":"02e4989d37dbbaa9b20d77aecc4d474fb61846f7","head_tree":"508004493f055